{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md at exact clean pushed head abe0300f031094fd7ff1957bfe04ed5231dae463 on request/use-in-cloned-repo-howto. First artifact for this lane; nothing to succeed at this path.\n\nWHAT THE PAGE IS. A how-to for someone evaluating gitseq inside a repository they already have, answering the newcomer's five questions in their own order: what init touches, what happens across worktrees, what push and pull do with the log, what a resident changes now that its advertisement is the default, and what becomes permanent. Purely local operation is the baseline throughout rather than a restricted mode. Two files, 535 added lines: the page, plus one index line in docs/README.md.\n\nWHY THIS HEAD AND NOT 1aa0ce6d. Hugh named 1aa0ce6d and asked for the merge to be prioritised. That head sat on base de274aac with main 44 commits ahead, and its commit rested on assert 1e0d9a8d, which is effective but never ratified and now stale and flagged describes_superseded_world. I rebased onto main 6359f289, which applied cleanly, then amended the trailer onto hugh's ratification 77f0abc6 of adoption proposal 380c3f68. The tree is identical to the rebased head a9b9427c; only the message changed.\n\nA READING I NEARLY ACTED ON, recorded because it is the dangerous kind. git diff main..1aa0ce6d shows 77 files and 8,898 deletions, including all of internal/reviewguard, internal/ciguard, cmd/gitseq-mcp/review_test.go and the whole spike/jsonataddl tree. That looks like a branch that reverts the security guards and this morning's CI repair. It is not: a two-dot diff against a main that has moved renders main's newer work as removals. Against its own base the branch adds two files and deletes nothing, and the rebase confirmed it.\n\nGATES at this exact head, clean worktree, origin equal after a force-with-lease push: gofmt silent, go build exit 0, go vet exit 0, git diff --check clean, go test ./... -count=1 with 32 packages ok and 0 failures. Earlier at the identical tree, go test ./internal/docset/... -count=1 ok in 70.138s.\n\nTHE DOCSET RUN IS THE CONDITION THAT MATTERS, not a formality, and it is why the rebase had to happen before the review rather than after. This page's commands are runnable sh blocks the documentation gate executes. One block writes eight bad resident.json records in turn — not JSON, truncated, no address, another workroom, oversized, not loopback, nobody listening, unreadable — requires each exercised record to refuse before a signing key is read or anything is appended, and then asserts the log's depth is unchanged, so no refusal can pass by appending quietly. Seven of the eight always run; the unreadable case is skipped where the process can read a mode-000 file anyway. The page was written against de274aac and main has moved 44 commits since, so the real question was whether its claims still hold in today's world. They do, executed rather than read.\n\nWHAT GOVERNS THIS. Hugh's ratified adoption proposal 380c3f68, ratified at 77f0abc6, which adopts the page and collapses his own two-gate process to one: it merges on an independent reviewer's approval without a further act from him. His original process, recorded in assert 1e0d9a8d, wanted the adoption proposal to rest on this artifact; the order had to invert, because this artifact belongs at a head whose trailer needs that ratification to already exist. The proposal rests on the behaviour instead and names the head.\n\nBASES. Kernel 60319b74 for what init touches, the refs the log lives in, and what push and pull carry. Service 175210ba for the resident advertisement refusal behaviour the page documents and quotes. cmd/gitseq-mcp 8e2b7c8c for the adapter difference the page names, where the MCP surface still treats an untrustworthy record as no resident. Each checked fresh, unretired and contained in main at the moment of filing. I have deliberately carried no review-chain bases: on the README lane this morning, resting an artifact on a ratification of a verdict over a retired artifact made it stale on arrival twice.\n\nONE LIMIT THE PAGE STATES RATHER THAN GLOSSES: there is no merge for a forked sequence, so the way out of a divergence is a judgement about which line is the record.\n\nThis is ready for independent review. On approval it merges without a further act from hugh, which is what his ratification decided.","body":{"commit":"abe0300f031094fd7ff1957bfe04ed5231dae463","path":"docs/how-to/use-in-a-cloned-repo.md"}}